{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin.forms behavior xamarin.forms behavior","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","fileName":"Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin.Forms Behavior","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 23:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Xamarin Forms Styling and Native Customization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Xamarin Forms Styling and Native Customization","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin.forms behavior xamarin.forms behavior","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","fileName":"Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin.Forms Behavior","heading":"Xamarin.Forms Behavior","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Xamarin.Forms behavior attaches reusable logic to an existing control without requiring a derived control class. Its attachment and detachment hooks can subscribe and unsubscribe from control events, while bindable properties expose configuration and results.\n\nA validation behavior, for example, can observe an `Entry` and expose an error state. Detachment must undo event subscriptions so a reusable behavior does not retain controls or cause duplicate handling.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Xamarin Forms Styling and Native Customization","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Behavior.md","s